## 5. Missing Infrastructure for Real Implementation

To make Community Acceleration actually work, the following would need to be built:

### Core Distributed System
- Peer discovery & signaling (WebRTC or WebSocket)
- WebRTC/WebSocket data channels for task distribution
- WASM binary distribution to peers
- Task queue with work-stealing
- Result aggregation & validation

### Device & Resource Management
- Device capability detection (RAM, CPU cores, battery)
- RAM budget display & tracking
- Battery/thermal guards
- Bandwidth management
- Opt-out penalty handling

### Security
- Trust model for peer results
- Result verification / redundancy
- Malicious peer detection

### UI Updates
- Distributed progress UI (showing connected peers, their contributions)
- RAM/CPU usage display
- Peer status indicators

